      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tungsten segregation will enhance grain-boundary cohesion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tungsten segregation will promote crack blunting.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reinforced grain boundaries will impede crack initiation and propagation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A tungsten concentration of approximately 1–2 at% will leave the magnetostructural transitions responsible for the caloric response largely unaffected.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tungsten-doped alloy will have greater load-bearing capacity than the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tungsten-doped alloy will have greater resistance to cracking than the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tungsten-doped alloy will retain adiabatic temperature change and isothermal entropy change comparable to those of the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefits apply during combined or separate magnetic-field and pressure-field operation at refrigeration temperatures.",
